exit=0
--- stdout ---
Encrypted appliance backups

Usage:
  loxicmd appliance backup [flags]
  loxicmd appliance backup [command]

Available Commands:
  create      Create an authenticated, encrypted backup archive
  key-create  Create a new root-only backup encryption key
  verify      Verify a backup archive without changing anything

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for backup

Global Flags:
  -s, --apiserver string    Set API server IP address (default "127.0.0.1")
      --bearer              Send the token as 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' (required by the inference gateway; disable for classic loxilb raw-token targets) (default true)
      --cacert string       CA certificate (PEM) to verify the server (https only)
      --cert string         Client certificate (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -k, --insecure            Skip TLS certificate verification (https only)
      --key string          Client private key (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -o, --output string       Set output layer (ex.) wide, json)
  -p, --port int            Set API server port number (default 11111)
      --protocol string     Set API server http/https (default "http")
  -t, --timeout int16       Set timeout (default 10)
      --token string        Set Token for the API server (deprecated: the value is visible in shell history and process listings; use --token-file)
      --token-file string   Read the API server token from an owner-only (0600) regular file; replaces the deprecated --token

Use "loxicmd appliance backup [command] --help" for more information about a command.
--- stderr ---
